WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.260
Speaker 1: We have yet another former Trump&nbsp;
staffer saying this is serious and Trump may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:14.940
end up in prison. Here is Mick Mulvaney, Donald&nbsp;
Trump's own former chief of staff previous to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:22.680
Mark Meadows, saying Trump indeed may end up&nbsp;
doing prison time. I don't even agree with this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.120
but this is Mick Mulvaney himself saying it.
Speaker 3: If Donald Trump had done what Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.680
Biden did here, what Mike Pence did here,&nbsp;
when they found their classified documents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:35.340
they gave them back and there's no charges&nbsp;
against Pence. There's not going to be charges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.260
against Biden. The difference here is what Trump&nbsp;
did to try and cover up what he did in the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.520
place. As is so often the case, it's not the&nbsp;
underlying crime, it's the interference. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.080
the cover up that gets folks in trouble. And they&nbsp;
have him with significant evidence, it looks like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:54.720
as to obstruction. So I think the chances of a&nbsp;
guilty verdict are fairly high and the chances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.360
of real jailtime are pretty high.
Speaker 2: And what do you say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.220
real jail time? How long might that be?
Speaker 3: Well, at his age, it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.520
really make much difference. Right. I think&nbsp;
the maximum, if you add up all the math,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.978
the maximum could be over 500 years.
Speaker 5: The minimum would be 100 year stop.&nbsp;

00:01:09.978 --> 00:01:15.900
Speaker 1: I don't even think I agree with Mick&nbsp;
Mulvaney. And I've said all along, I don't believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:24.240
Donald Trump will do a day of prison time period.&nbsp;
However, I will say that over the last 72 hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:34.560
I have moved ever so slightly in the direction&nbsp;
of maybe, maybe there will be some jail time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.220
for Trump. It's it's I'm now in the realm of&nbsp;
before I was in absolutely no way in hell.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:49.200
After speaking to a couple of lawyers, reading&nbsp;
through the indictment, reading about the law&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.880
around the allegations for which Trump is going&nbsp;
to be charged. Looking at a few different things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:00.780
I am now, I've moved from no way in hell Trump&nbsp;
does prison time to. It is extremely unlikely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.680
but possible, that Trump ends up&nbsp;
with something. It could, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.780
end up being one of these. Well, he will serve&nbsp;
it at his house with an ankle monitor, which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.740
by the way, I would still accept at this&nbsp;
point in time. All right. So Mick Mulvaney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.880
also now on the list of former Trump&nbsp;
staffers who says this is serious and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.200
Trump could be toast. To quote William Barr,&nbsp;
we'll see who else comes out of the woodwork.

